  "facts": [
    "Opened December 6, 2015, the Abraham Lincoln Bridge instantly added six northbound lanes to I‑65, doubling the corridor’s capacity and relieving congestion that had plagued downtown Louisville for decades.",
    "Its 700‑foot main span, a sleek cable‑stayed design with a single A‑shaped tower, stretches 2,100 feet across the Ohio River, making it a striking modern landmark beside the historic Kennedy Bridge.",
    "Tolling began December 30, 2016, after a public‑involvement process that used 3D visualizations and real‑time polling to shape the bridge’s final aesthetic and functional features."
